{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azure-sdk/azure-mcp","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:08.734Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azure-sdk/azure-mcp/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azure-sdk/azure-mcp/about"},"readme":"# About\n\nThis repository contains the official container images for the Azure MCP server. You can use Docker to run a standalone Linux container with the Azure MCP server and connect it to an MCP client.\n\n# Featured Tags\n\n- `latest` ```docker pull mcr.microsoft.com/azure-sdk/azure-mcp```\n\n# Configuration\n\nYou must also have Docker installed locally. Docker provides packages that easily configure Docker on any Mac, Windows, or Linux system.\n\n# How to Use This Image\n\n```\ndocker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/azure-sdk/azure-mcp:<version>\n```\n\n# Support\n\nView issues related to this image in our GitHub repository [here](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/issues).\n\nIf you encounter any bugs or security issues with the tool, please file an issue in our [GitHub repo](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/issues/new/choose)\n\n# License\nFor more information visit the [MAR Legal Notice](https://github.com/microsoft/containerregistry/blob/main/legal/Container-Images-Legal-Notice.md)\n\nSee license terms [here](https://github.com/Azure/azure-mcp/blob/main/LICENSE)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-09-24T23:13:54.7296988+00:00","categories":["MCP"],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"800K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"3.0.0-beta.47","digest":"sha256:b7970d9707c7e4c82ad069060f4f66fd3d479c09a61254b4b13243f84213c4d5","pushed":"2026-09-24T23:13:56.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"applicatio